<%# One pool and the rules that fill it. Locals: `group` (BudgetPagePresenter::Group) and `band`
    (the account it sits in — the card is a row of that band's drag list).

    The header says how the pool is doing in the app's ONE row vocabulary
    (`HomeHelper#pool_status_label`, spec §4.4) — the same words, the same red, as Home and the
    distribution screen. A second vocabulary here would have two screens describe one envelope
    differently on the same afternoon.

    `priority` is stated because this page is where funding priority is set; the number is what
    decides who gets filled first when the money runs out, and dragging this card — or its ▲▼ —
    is what writes it. %>
<% status = group.status %>
<section class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded"
         data-pool-group="<%= group.pool.name %>"
         data-pool-id="<%= group.pool.id %>"
         data-app--budget-page--reorder-target="row"
         draggable="true"
         data-action="dragstart->app--budget-page--reorder#start
                      dragend->app--budget-page--reorder#finish">
  <div class="px-6 py-3 border-b border-gray-200 flex justify-between items-baseline gap-4">
    <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3">
      <%= render "reorder_controls", group: group, band: band %>
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900"><%= group.pool.name %></h3>
      <span class="text-xs text-gray-400">priority <%= group.priority %></span>
    </div>
    <span class="text-sm <%= status.needs_attention? ? "text-status-danger font-medium" : "text-gray-700" %>">
      <%# `period_closed:` is not optional here. The suffix says WHICH PERIOD the figure belongs
          to, and a swept rate-rule envelope reading `$400.00 left · last period` on Home while
          this page reads `$400.00 left` for the same pool on the same afternoon is two screens
          describing one envelope differently. Off the status's own memoised calculator, so this
          page still builds exactly one calculator per pool. %>
      <%= pool_status_label(status, period_closed: status.period_closed?) %>
      <span class="text-gray-400"><%= budget_group_balance(group) %></span>
    </span>
  </div>

  <% group.rules.each do |rule| %>
    <%= render "rule_row", rule: rule %>
  <% end %>
</section>
